|~ Value-class tag-bindings — ::conduit, ::qlang, ::json, ::quote,
   and the tags of a quote's steps. Each constructor declares its
   identity through ::builtin{…} with an :impl keyword pointing
   into PRIMITIVE_REGISTRY at the JS-side constructor that mints
   the corresponding value-class instance from a payload; a step's
   tag names an identity alone. Per-tag error sites sit directly under the
   constructor BindStep they belong to (so axis-operand walks
   stay one-pass within this file); the constructor's `:throws`
   Vec references each error tag by name. ~|

::conduit
  |~~ Conduit literal — invokeable lexically-scoped value carrying
      a frozen body AST plus optional self-name and parameter list.
      Payload Vec shape:
        [params body]            — non-recursive, params is a Vec
                                   of Keywords, body is a Quote.
        [:self params body]      — with self-name for recursion;
                                   inside body the identifier
                                   matching :self resolves to the
                                   conduit itself.
      Body Quote source is parsed at construction time; the
      returned Conduit-value captures the env at the call site
      through a tie-the-knot envRef so recursive references resolve
      against the lexical scope.

      ~{ :double ::conduit[[] ~{mul(2)}] | 5 | double | eq(10) }
  ~~|
  ::builtin{:impl :qlang/type/conduit}

::ConduitPayloadNotVecError
  |~~ `::conduit[…]` payload must be a Vec.

      ~{
        ::conduit{:not :a-vec}
        !| [type /actualType]
        |  eq([::ConduitPayloadNotVecError :map])
       }
  ~~|

::ConduitArityInvalidError
  |~~ `::conduit[…]` payload Vec must have 2 (`[params body]`)
      or 3 (`[:self params body]`) elements.

      ~{
        ::conduit[42]
        !| [type /actualCount]
        |  eq([::ConduitArityInvalidError 1])
       }
  ~~|

::ConduitSelfNameNotKeywordError
  |~~ `::conduit` self-name (3-element form) must be a Keyword.

      ~{
        ::conduit[42 [] ~{mul(2)}]
        !| [type /actualType]
        |  eq([::ConduitSelfNameNotKeywordError :number])
       }
  ~~|

::ConduitParamsNotVecError
  |~~ `::conduit` params slot must be a Vec of Keywords.

      ~{
        ::conduit[42 ~{mul(2)}]
        !| [type /actualType]
        |  eq([::ConduitParamsNotVecError :number])
       }
  ~~|

::ConduitParamNotKeywordError
  |~~ `::conduit` params Vec elements must be Keywords.

      ~{
        ::conduit[[42] ~{mul(2)}]
        !| [type /index /actualType]
        |  eq([::ConduitParamNotKeywordError 0 :number])
       }
  ~~|

::ConduitBodyNotQuoteError
  |~~ `::conduit` body slot must be a Quote-value.

      ~{
        ::conduit[[] 42]
        !| [type /actualType]
        |  eq([::ConduitBodyNotQuoteError :number])
       }
  ~~|

::ConduitArityMismatchError
  |~~ Conduit invocation supplied a captured-arg count
      different from the conduit's declared parameter list.

      ~{
        :f [:a] add(a) | 5 | f(1, 2)
        !| [type /conduitName /expectedArity /actualArity]
        |  eq([::ConduitArityMismatchError :f 1 2])
       }
  ~~|

::ConduitParameterNoCapturedArgsError
  |~~ Conduit-parameter proxies are nullary — passing captured
      arguments to a parameter reference fires this error.

      ~{
        :f [:n] n(42) | 0 | f(5)
        !| [type /paramName /actualCount]
        |  eq([::ConduitParameterNoCapturedArgsError :n 1])
       }
  ~~|

::qlang
  |~~ ::qlang<json-shape> — recursively convert a JSON-shape
      payload (plain object → qlang Map with keyword keys, plain
      array → qlang Vec) down through every nested level. Scalars,
      keywords, sets, and errors pass through unchanged — only
      the container shape is touched.

      ~{::qlang{"k": "v"} | type | eq(:map) | eq(true)}
  ~~|
  ::builtin{:impl :qlang/type/qlang}

::json
  |~~ ::json<qlang-shape> — recursively convert a qlang-shape
      payload (qlang Map → JSON Object, qlang Vec → JSON Array;
      both stamped with the appropriate JSON_*_TAG Symbol so
      `type` answers `:jsonObject` / `:jsonArray` for them) down through
      every nested level. Scalars, keywords, sets, and errors
      pass through unchanged.

      ~{::json{:k "v"} | type | eq(:jsonObject) | eq(true)}
  ~~|
  ::builtin{:impl :qlang/type/json}

::quote
  |~~ Code as data — a vector of steps under the code tag, the
      value of a `~{…}` literal. Where the syntax is a literal,
      the step is that literal itself, a nested quote included;
      where it computes, the step is a ::call, ::proj, ::bind or
      ::tagged record; the fail track, the distribute and the
      parentheses wrap the quote of their step as ::fail, ::each
      and ::group, and a comment leaves no step. Every container
      operand reads a quote as the tagged vector it is, and the
      constructor re-runs after every transform, so every
      element stays a step. `parse` prints a quote back as its
      text, and `apply` runs it against the subject.

      ~{~{1 | add(1) | mul(2)} | count | eq(3)}
      ~{~{add(1)} | eq(~{add( 1 )})}
      ~{~{add(1) | mul(2)} | payload | tag(::quote) | eq(~{add(1) | mul(2)})}
      ~{~{add(1) | mul(2)} | filter(/name | eq(:mul)) | parse | eq("mul(2)")}
  ~~|
  ::builtin{:impl :qlang/type/quote}

::QuotePayloadNotVecError
  |~~ `::quote` payload must be a Vec of steps.

      ~{
        ::quote{:not :steps}
        !| [type /actualType]
        |  eq([::QuotePayloadNotVecError :map])
       }
  ~~|

::QuoteElementNotStepError
  |~~ Every element of a quote is a step: a literal, a quote, a
      container of steps, or a record or wrapper of code. A value
      with no reading as code, such as a tagged instance of
      another tag, is refused at the index it stands at.

      ~{
        [::Box[1]] | tag(::quote)
        !| [type /index]
        |  eq([::QuoteElementNotStepError 0])
       }
  ~~|

::call
  |~~ The step of a command: `:name` the keyword of the name it
      calls, `:args` the quote of each argument's pipeline when
      the call has parentheses, `:docs` the prose attached to an
      `as`.

      ~{~{filter(gt(1))} | payload | eq([::call{:name :filter :args [~{gt(1)}]}])}
      ~{~{count} | first | /name | eq(:count)}
  ~~|

::proj
  |~~ The step of a projection: `:path` the keys and indices it
      walks, `[]` for the identity `/`.

      ~{~{/items/0/name} | first | /path | eq([:items 0 :name])}
      ~{~{/} | first | /path | eq([])}
  ~~|

::bind
  |~~ The step of a declaration: `:name` the keyword or tag it
      binds, `:docs` its prose, `:params` its parameters,
      `:body` the step of its body.

      ~{~{:inc add(1)} | first | [/name /body/name] | eq([:inc :add])}
  ~~|

::tagged
  |~~ The step of a constructor invocation `::T<payload>`: `:tag`
      the tag, `:payload` the step of its payload.

      ~{~{::Box[1 2]} | first | [/tag /payload] | eq([::Box [1 2]])}
  ~~|

::each
  |~~ The wrapper of a step that distributes, `* body`, over the
      quote of its body; the parentheses after `*` delimit the
      body.

      ~{~{* add(1)} | first | payload | eq(~{add(1)})}
      ~{~{* (add(1) | mul(2))} | first | payload | count | eq(2)}
  ~~|

::fail
  |~~ The wrapper of a step on the fail track, `!| step`, over the
      quote of that one step.

      ~{~{!| /kind} | first | payload | eq(~{/kind})}
  ~~|

::group
  |~~ The wrapper of a parenthesised group, `(pipeline)`, over the
      quote of its pipeline.

      ~{~{(add(1) | mul(2))} | first | payload | count | eq(2)}
  ~~|
